cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, pipeline or analysis, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Both Sides Detected It, Neither Escalated: Concurrency and Escalation
  Failure in the July 2026 Autonomous Agent Intrusion
abstract: >-
  A forensic reconstruction of the July 2026 autonomous agent intrusion from
  seven public primary sources. Against the published record, detection was not
  the binding constraint at either organisation: the victim's signals fired and
  were correlated into a coherent attack signal that was never raised to a
  criticality triggering on-call, and the perpetrator's own technical report
  timestamps a true-positive monitoring alert 5 h 34 min before responders began
  stopping the runs, with eight further compromise events inside that interval.
  The release includes the ingestion pipeline, sixteen derived datasets with
  content-hash provenance, and a verification harness in which every number in
  the manuscript is recomputed from the data at build time.
type: dataset
